 that still exist. The Moth Snowstorm records in painful detail this rapid dissolution of nature's abundance and proposes a radical solution: that we recognize our capacity to love the natural world. Arguing that neither sustainable development nor ecosystem services have proven adequate as defenses against pollution, habitat destruction, species degradation, and climate change, McCarthy asks us to consider nature as an intrinsic good and an emotional and spiritual resource, capable of inspiring joy, wonder, and even love.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-the-moth-snowstorm-michael-mccarthy.jpg","displaySummary":"The Moth Snowstorm records in painful detail this rapid dissolution of nature's abundance and proposes a radical solution: that we recognize our capacity to love the natural world. Arguing that neither sustainable development nor ecosystem services have proven adequate as defenses against pollution, habitat destruction, species degradation, and climate change, McCarthy asks us to consider nature as an intrinsic good and an emotional and spiritual resource, capable of inspiring joy, wonder, and even love.","primarySubject":"Nature & Environment","primaryTopic":"Climate, Weather & Disaster","subjectEvidence":{"primarySubject":"Nature & Environment","confidence":"medium","method":"evidence_score","candidates":[{"subject":"Nature & Environment","score":54,"evidenceCount":9},{"subject":"Society & Culture","score":5,"evidenceCount":1}],"evidence":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Environmental degradation","mappedSubject":"Nature & Environment","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-moth-snowstorm-michael-mccarthy","id":"subject-evidence-book-the-moth-snowstorm-michael-mccarthy-1"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","rawLabel":"Nature","mappedSubject":"Nature & Environment","score":6,"confidence":"high","sourceId":"source-open-library-the-moth-snowstorm-michael-mccarthy","id":"